---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How the upstream checks work
    accDescr: The workflow Upstream runs two checks of what the extension relies on but doesn't control. Every morning, autodarts-contract takes the expected values from src/autodarts.ts and asks the real Autodarts with made-up data only, about a dozen requests: it looks for the key of the session, the sign-in service and the client in the code of play.autodarts.com, script by script until it has found all three, follows the forward of play.autodarts.io, and sends a made-up token, a made-up account and the end of a made-up session to the sign-in service, through the functions of the extension. Every morning as well, chrome-beta downloads Chrome for Testing Beta, the next version of Chrome, and runs the end-to-end tests in it against the fake Autodarts. When either fails, its summary names what changed and where the code relies on it, and the bot-health bot opens an issue with the label bot-failure, which the next run that passes closes.

    workflow["The workflow Upstream<br>also for a pull request that changes it<br>or src/autodarts.ts"]

    subgraph daily ["autodarts-contract, every morning"]
        direction TB
        values["The expected values<br>from src/autodarts.ts"]
        page["play.autodarts.com and its scripts<br>the key of the session, the sign-in service<br>and the client, until all three are found"]
        forward["play.autodarts.io<br>forwards to play.autodarts.com"]
        auth["api.autodarts.com/auth/v1<br>a made-up token and account are refused<br>with 400 or 401, a session ends"]
        values --> page
        page --> forward
        forward --> auth
    end

    subgraph beta ["chrome-beta, every morning"]
        direction TB
        download["scripts/chrome-for-testing.sh<br>Chrome for Testing Beta,<br>about four weeks ahead of the players"]
        tests["The end-to-end tests of test/e2e/<br>in Beta, against the fake Autodarts"]
        download --> tests
    end

    workflow --> values
    workflow --> download

    report["The summary of the check<br>what changed and every place<br>of the code that relies on it"]
    auth --> report
    tests --> report

    issue["bot-health opens an issue<br>with the label bot-failure;<br>the next run that passes closes it"]
    report -->|on a failure| issue

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    class workflow bot
    class issue person
